Iqbal (an Indian subcontinent poet who died in 1938) described this dire situation in his poetry (بانگ درا) as follows:

@rtl-ur لے گئے تثلیث کے فرزند میراثِ خلیل  خشتِ بنيادِ كليسا بن گئی خاكِ حجاز


@color-amber Europe took away the (intellectual) heritage of Muslims  And (from it,) built the foundation of European empire


